name: sim.multiplyPoses
description: Multiplies two poses
luaSynopsis: list resultPose = sim.multiplyPoses(list poseIn1, list poseIn2)
pythonSynopsis: float[7] resultPose = sim.multiplyPoses(float[7] poseIn1, float[7] poseIn2)
inputs:
1. poseIn1: first input pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
2. poseIn2: second input pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
outputs:
1. resultPose: the result pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
replacedBy:
- use simEigen methods
